       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses of this size can also cause shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nCould this be a typo? Here are the usual options:\n- **5 mg PO daily** is the usual starting dose. It's also used for frail or older patients.\n- **10 mg PO daily** is the maximum dose.\n\nIf you meant 30 mg on purpose, for example because of a specialist recommendation, tell me the reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
